The bug was caused by the `_gnutls_resolve_priorities()` function returning a string that was allocated using standard memory allocation functions (`malloc()`) instead of the GnuTLS-specific memory functions (`gnutls_malloc()`). This inconsistency could lead to memory management issues, such as memory leaks or improper deallocation, since the caller would not be using the appropriate deallocation function (`gnutls_free()`) to free the allocated memory.

